    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d845">

                <pb facs="0919" n="1753" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1753"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 862.85/610</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Argentina</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Stimson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-11-09T19:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 9, 1918, 7 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your October 26, 12 noon. Department learns that British Minister has been
                    instructed to notify Argentine Government that his Government will not approve
                    voyage of <hi rendition="#italic">Bahia Blanca</hi> until an opportunity is
                    afforded them to examine the terms of transfer to Argentine flag. You will
                    support your British colleague’s representations in this matter and will make it
                    quite clear to the Argentine Government that this Government would reserve all
                    its rights as a belligerent should the proposed voyage of the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Bahia Blanca</hi> actually <pb facs="0920" n="1754"
                        xml:id="pg1754"/> take place. Department unable to understand Minister of
                    Foreign Affairs’ statement that since matter has been arranged with Naón, United States Government
                    now makes no objection to proposed voyage, in view of fact that Naón has never spoken to
                    Department specifically in regard to <hi rendition="#italic">Bahia Blanca</hi>.
                    So inform British colleague.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
